DataStage XML Column Lineage Extractor — COMPLETE INTERACTIVE VERSION
================================================================================

DESCRIPTION:
    Reads IBM DataStage exported job XML (.dsx / .xml) and generates an Excel
    report tracing every target column back to its source, capturing all
    transformation logic along the way.

    This script satisfies EVERY DataStage XML parsing requirement:
      - Interactive console menu to select XML files
      - Handles ALL stage types per IBM documentation
      - Handles column renames in middle stages
      - Handles derived columns (new columns created in stages)
      - Handles pass-through columns
      - Captures record filtering/loss logic
      - Case-insensitive column matching
      - Traces backwards: Target -> Logic -> Source

EXCEL OUTPUT COLUMNS:
    Source Column Name | Source Data Type | Extraction Logic | Target Column Name | Target Data Type

HOW TO USE:
    1. Place this script in the same folder as your DataStage XML/DSX files
    2. Run: python ds_lineage_complete.py
    3. Select the XML file from the numbered menu
    4. Excel file is auto-generated as: {filename}_lineage.xlsx

